---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Simon"
  description="Simon is a private, personal chief-of-staff productivity system built and operated by Logan Lyle for his own use."
>
  <div class="eyebrow">Simon / Chief of Staff</div>
  <h1>Simon — Personal Chief of Staff</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Simon is a private, personal productivity system I built and use for my own
    chief-of-staff work — calendar, email triage, task tracking, and daily briefings
    across accounts I personally own and operate.
  </p>

  <p><strong>This is not a public product.</strong> It isn't available to anyone else, and
    it doesn't manage data on behalf of anyone other than me.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>What Simon does</h2>
    <ul class="check">
      <li>Reads and organizes information from Google services I've explicitly
        connected — Gmail, Calendar, and Drive — to help me track commitments,
        follow-ups, and my schedule.</li>
      <li>Occasionally takes actions I've explicitly pre-authorized, such as sending a
        daily summary email to my own inbox.</li>
      <li>Runs on infrastructure I control, using Anthropic's Claude models to process
        and reason over that information.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What Simon doesn't do</h2>
    <ul class="check">
      <li>Doesn't sell data, in any form, to anyone.</li>
      <li>Doesn't use data for advertising or build advertising profiles.</li>
      <li>Doesn't share data with third parties, other than the infrastructure and API
        providers required to run it.</li>
      <li>Doesn't act on, or gain access to, any account I haven't explicitly
        connected.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Access &amp; revocation</h2>
    <p>
      Because Simon connects through standard Google OAuth, I can review or revoke its
      access at any time from my Google Account's
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Security → Third-party access
      </a> settings, the same as any other connected app.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:hello@jloganlyle.com">hello@jloganlyle.com</a>
      <span class="needs-input">confirm address</span>
    </p>
    <p><a href="/privacy">Read the full Privacy Policy →</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
